KZ2 patch 6019: label-release wake. Every label write of the FIFO walker (NV406E
SEMAPHORE_RELEASE in cellGcmSys.c's drain, NV4097 0x1D70/0x1D74 back-end releases in rsx_commands.c) calls
cellGcm_label_notify(): a sequence number goes up and, only when a host thread waits, a condition variable is
broadcast. cellGcm_label_seq() / cellGcm_label_wait_seq(seq, timeout_ms) let a host-side label wait sleep until the
next release instead of polling with sys_timer_usleep (KZ2's Renderer::WaitLabel 0x48AE8 polls label 0x4B with
usleep(30), about 16,700 calls per second in the level; its host replacement is in port/kz2/kz2_ppu_overrides.cpp).
The timeout keeps a waiter correct when a label is written by another path (it re-checks the label then).
Win32 SRW lock + condition variable, pthread elsewhere. Upstream candidate (general; no title-specific part).
v0.17.0 rebase (ps3recomp a6d76c8): 6019 label notify after #401's RELEASE get publish and in upstream's FEED0001 host-buffer semaphore path.

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.18.0: context and offsets only.

